A mount takes a CapTable capability without the right to write the table,
so a process comes to name the capabilities of a table its holder was let to read and nothing more,
where only one that may write a table makes it a process's.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: process's table slot without the right to write the table

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -459,7 +459,7 @@ static int op_process(struct thread *t, const struct cap *cap,
         return process_uninstall(proc, arg[1]);
     case OP_PROCESS_MOUNT: {
         struct cap tc;
-        int err = slot_lookup_typed(t, arg[2], CAP_CAPTABLE, RIGHT_W, &tc);
+        int err = slot_lookup_typed(t, arg[2], CAP_CAPTABLE, 0, &tc);
         if (err != KERR_OK) {
             return err;
         }
